    {
      "id": "nl-cap-r2-q1",
      "round": 2,
      "type": "numeric",
      "prompt": "A junction stores \\(Q_j(V)=-Q_0\\sqrt{1-V/\\phi_b}\\) with \\(Q_0=2\\ \\mathrm{pC}\\), \\(\\phi_b=0.8\\ \\mathrm{V}\\) (reader Eq. 4.29 form). What is its small-signal capacitance at \\(V=-2\\ \\mathrm{V}\\), in pF?",
      "answer": 0.668153,
      "unit": "pF",
      "tolerance": 0.02,
      "explanation": "\\(C=\\dfrac{dQ_j}{dV}=\\dfrac{Q_0}{2\\phi_b\\sqrt{1-V/\\phi_b}}\\) (Eq. 4.30). At \\(V=-2\\): \\(\\sqrt{1+2.5}=1.871\\), so \\(C=\\dfrac{2\\ \\mathrm{pC}}{1.6\\ \\mathrm{V}\\times1.871}=0.6682\\ \\mathrm{pF}\\).",
