    {
      "id": "nl-cap-r3-q1",
      "round": 3,
      "type": "mc",
      "prompt": "The junction above is biased at \\(-2\\ \\mathrm{V}\\) and driven by a 1 V-amplitude signal. Is \\(q=C(-2\\ \\mathrm{V})\\cdot v\\) still accurate?",
      "options": [
        "Yes: the small-signal capacitance works for any amplitude",
        "No: the Taylor expansion assumes \\(|v|\\) is small compared with the scale over which \\(C\\) changes; a 1 V swing changes \\(C\\) noticeably, so the charge response is distorted",
        "Yes, as long as the signal is a sine wave",
        "No, because the capacitance becomes negative"
      ],
      "correct_index": 1,
      "explanation": "The small-signal model keeps only the linear term of \\(f(V_0+v)\\) (reader Eq. 4.24). With \\(|v|\\) comparable to \\(|V_0-\\phi_b|\\), higher-order terms matter: the charge is a distorted copy of the voltage. 'Small' means small enough that the slope is nearly constant over the swing.",
      "figure": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 330 140\" role=\"img\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\"><title>Large swing on a curved Q–V</title><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"310\" y2=\"20\" stroke-opacity=\"0.5\"/><text x=\"310\" y=\"34\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">V</text><polyline points=\"30,120 34.7,119.2 39.3,118.4 44,117.6 48.7,116.8 53.3,115.9 58,115.1 62.7,114.2 67.3,113.4 72,112.5 76.7,111.7 81.3,110.8 86,109.9 90.7,109 95.3,108.1 100,107.2 104.7,106.3 109.3,105.4 114,104.4 118.7,103.5 123.3,102.5 128,101.5 132.7,100.5 137.3,99.5 142,98.5 146.7,97.5 151.3,96.5 156,95.4 160.7,94.3 165.3,93.3 170,92.2 174.7,91.1 179.3,89.9 184,88.8 188.7,87.6 193.3,86.4 198,85.2 202.7,84 207.3,82.7 212,81.4 216.7,80.1 221.3,78.7 226,77.4 230.7,76 235.3,74.5 240,73 244.7,71.5 249.3,69.9 254,68.3 258.7,66.6 263.3,64.9 268,63.1 272.7,61.2 277.3,59.2 282,57.1 286.7,54.9 291.3,52.5 296,49.9 300.7,47.1 305.3,44 310,40.4\" stroke-width=\"2.2\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"14\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Q</text><line x1=\"101.3\" y1=\"107.7\" x2=\"202.1\" y2=\"85.1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><circle cx=\"151.7\" cy=\"96.4\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><text x=\"202.1\" y=\"79.1\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">slope = C</text></svg>",
      "figure_alt": "Junction Q-V curve with a tangent at -2 V."
